Dynamica is availabe for Max now.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>This is an excellent fix <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":)" title="Smile"><br><br>Thank you VicariousEnt, now I need to dig up the code I saw on converting a rigid body to a btBvhTriangleMeshShape and I am in serious buisness!  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_cool.gif" width="15" height="15" alt="8)" title="Cool"></div></blockquote>The last release of Dyamica actually has code in it for this but a bug kept it from being exposed in the released build. If you're up to building the Maya Dynamica project yourself, change this line in collisionShapeNode.cpp...<br><br>fnEnumAttr.addField("BvhMesh", 6); &lt;-- Line 71 in collisionShapeNode::initialize()<br> <br>Change the 6 to a 7 and it will work. That change is necesary for the changes made just before release but has been fixed in the very latest trunk. See my issue page for more details...<br><br><a href="http://code.google.com/p/dynamica/issues/detail?id=18" class="postlink">http://code.google.com/p/dynamica/issues/detail?id=18</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7272">VicariousEnt</a> — Tue Sep 13, 2011 4:22 am</p><hr />
